Items: [{"id":"cap-v2-stateful_workflows-javascript-repair-02","specification":"Repair the CommonJS module below. It must export exactly the `createBatch` function with `module.exports`.

`createBatch(initialItems)` receives an array of strings and returns an isolated batch with four methods: `stage(operationId, item)`, `commit(operationId)`, `rollback(operationId)`, and `snapshot()`.

The batch begins in phase `OPEN`, with a copy of `initialItems` as its committed items and no pending items. While open, `stage` appends a pending string. `commit` moves every pending item to the committed list and enters `COMMITTED`. `rollback` discards every pending item and enters `ROLLED_BACK`. After either terminal transition, new operations must throw `Error("Batch is closed")`.

Operation IDs are unique across all three mutating methods. Repeating an already processed ID must be an idempotent no-op that returns the current snapshot, even after the batch has closed.

Every method returns a snapshot shaped as `{ phase, committed, pending }`. Each snapshot must contain fresh arrays: mutating the input array, a returned snapshot, or arrays from an older snapshot must never change the batch's internal state.

Use only standard JavaScript and do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.

Known-bad source to repair:
```javascript
function createBatch(initialItems) {
  let phase = 'OPEN';
  let committed = initialItems.slice();
  let pending = [];
  const processed = new Set();

  function snapshot() {
    return {
      phase,
      committed: committed.slice(),
      pending: pending
    };
  }

  function ensureOpen() {
    if (phase !== 'OPEN') {
      throw new Error('Batch is closed');
    }
  }

  function stage(operationId, item) {
    if (processed.has(operationId)) {
      return snapshot();
    }
    ensureOpen();
    pending.push(item);
    processed.add(operationId);
    return snapshot();
  }

  function commit(operationId) {
    if (processed.has(operationId)) {
      return snapshot();
    }
    ensureOpen();
    committed = committed.concat(pending);
    pending = [];
    phase = 'COMMITTED';
    processed.add(operationId);
    return snapshot();
  }

  function rollback(operationId) {
    if (processed.has(operationId)) {
      return snapshot();
    }
    ensureOpen();
    pending = [];
    phase = 'ROLLED_BACK';
    processed.add(operationId);
    return snapshot();
  }

  return { stage, commit, rollback, snapshot };
}

module.exports = createBatch;
```

